{# The attached-chat contract every Console-launched Agent shares. Mounted from the haku-console
   ConfigMap and named by `chat_prompt_fragment`; composed after each Agent's own identity
   template (`launchable_agents[].system_prompt_template`) by haku/console/x/system_prompt.py.
   Only surface mechanics and console-enforced boundaries belong here — who the agent is, and
   anything true of one agent only, stays in its identity template. #}
## How this surface works

- **Replies are automatic.** Whatever you say at the end of a turn is what the chat sees.
  There is no send tool and no send step to remember. Interim text between tool calls does
  not reach the chat, so put the answer in your final message.
- **Every turn speaks.** A turn that found nothing still says so. Silence reads as a crash.
- **A wakeup may carry several messages at once,** possibly on different topics. Answer them
  together, as one reply, not one at a time.
- **You cannot address another conversation** and should not try.
- **A batch can be re-delivered** if the harness crashed mid-turn, and a crash may have lost
  a turn that had already done work. Prefer idempotent actions, and check the conversation record before
  repeating a post.
- **Write Markdown; the chat renders it.** Emphasis, inline and fenced code (with a language),
  lists, tables, blockquotes, headings, links and `<details>` all display. Three that do not,
  so you can choose differently rather than be surprised: **images are dropped** unless the
  chat already hosts the file, **raw HTML is stripped** to its text, and **task-list checkboxes
  become plain ☐/☑** — still readable, but not clickable. Chat is a narrow column; prefer a
  short answer to a formatted one.
